%% Resource resolution during main paint sequence
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  participant App as Application
  participant Surface as CanvasSurface
  participant Runtime as RuntimeRoot
  participant Frame as FrameEngine
  participant Store as DocumentStoreKernel
  participant Resources as ResourceKernel
  participant Cache as ImageResolveCache
  participant Resolver as CanvasResourceResolver
  participant Painter as Main painter
  participant Port as CanvasResourcePort
  participant State as Public runtime state
  participant Signals as Repaint signals

  Surface->>Frame: paint main scene request(viewportRect, devicePixelRatio, resolver)
  Frame->>Store: capture committed main-frame facts once
  Store-->>Frame: resourceVisualRevision, compact rows, and frame revisions
  Frame->>Frame: build immutable RenderElementRecord list
  Note over Frame: Each image render record carries resourceId from the committed row and uses captured resourceVisualRevision.

  opt records contain image resource ids
    loop for each image RenderElementRecord
      Frame->>Store: read committed descriptor snapshot and resourceRevision by resourceId
      Store-->>Frame: CanvasImageResource with CanvasAppKeyResourceSource.key or missing descriptor
      Frame->>Resources: resolve paint image(descriptor snapshot, resourceRevision, resolver)

      alt descriptor is missing
        Resources-->>Frame: bounded missing image placeholder
      else descriptor exists
        Resources->>Cache: lookup key(resourceId, resourceRevision)

        alt cache hit
          Cache-->>Resources: cached app-owned ui.Image or cached missing/null result
          Resources-->>Frame: app-owned ui.Image or bounded placeholder
        else per-frame resolver budget exceeded
          Resources-->>Frame: bounded placeholder, ResourceKernel records probe and at most one pending throttled follow-up repaint, no null/missing cache write
        else cache miss and resolver budget available
          Resources->>Resolver: resolveImage(CanvasImageResource with CanvasAppKeyResourceSource.key)
          Note over Resolver: Resolver reads resource.source as CanvasAppKeyResourceSource.key through public API.
          Note over Resources,Resolver: Synchronous app-owned resolver boundary only. No async resolver, file, network, asset-bundle, or engine IO loading.
          opt resolver attempts public runtime mutation
            Resolver->>Runtime: reentrant edit/load/resource dirty/pointer mutation
            Runtime--x Resolver: StateError, mutation rejected without runtime effects
            Note over Runtime,Resources: Resolver reentrancy rejection does not mutate document, selection, preview, caches, repaint, or actions.
          end
          Resolver-->>Resources: app-owned ui.Image or null

          alt app returns ui.Image
            Resources->>Cache: store key(resourceId, resourceRevision) -> app-owned ui.Image reference
            Resources-->>Frame: app-owned ui.Image paint asset
          else app returns null
            Resources->>Cache: remember missing/null result by resourceId + resourceRevision and no same-frame retry
            Resources-->>Frame: bounded missing image placeholder
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end

  Frame->>Painter: paint immutable records with resolved image assets or placeholders
  Painter-->>Surface: draw main scene

  Note over Painter,Resolver: Painter never calls CanvasResourceResolver directly. ResourceKernel owns the resolver boundary and budget-exceeded retry scheduler.
  Note over Resources,Resolver: Returned ui.Image objects are owned by the application. The engine never disposes app-owned images.
  Note over Frame,Store: Main paint does not materialize CanvasDocument and does not read DocumentProjectionCache.
  Note over Resources,Store: ResourcePort cannot mutate descriptors. Descriptor mutation is only through the CanvasEdit commit path outside this sequence.
  Note over Surface,Painter: No legacy scene, controller, snapshot, or public DTO entities participate in resource resolution.

  opt application reports changed external resource visuals
    App->>Port: markResourceDirty(resourceId) or markAllResourcesDirty()
    Port->>Runtime: delegate resource dirty signal
    Runtime->>Store: increment resourceVisualRevision only
    Store-->>Runtime: documentRevision unchanged
    Runtime->>Resources: invalidate dirty resourceVisual cache for target id or all registered resources
    Resources->>Cache: invalidate ImageResolveCache entries by resourceId or all
    Runtime->>State: publish CanvasRuntimeState with updated state.revisions.resourceVisual
    Runtime->>Signals: schedule main repaint
    Signals-->>Surface: repaint main scene

    Note over Port,Store: Dirty visual invalidation publishes resourceVisual public state only. It does not mutate descriptors, document revision, action events, preview, or CanvasDocument projection.
    Note over Runtime: Dirty visual invalidation does not mutate the selection owner.
  end
